### The 48 card entries against the 45 exposed tools

`docs/tool_cards/` holds **48** files and `alloagent/exposed_tools.txt` lists the **45**
tools that arm D actually exposes. The three entries that are not exposed tools:

| the card | what it is | why it is not an exposed tool |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/tool_cards/T_template.md` | the **template** the other cards are written from (`# T<id> <tool_name>`) | not a tool at all; it is the scaffold `docs/tool_cards/T_template.md` tells the author to copy |
| `docs/tool_cards/P6_fetch_allosteric_residue_potential.md` | the tool `fetch_allosteric_residue_potential` | it is registered but **not exposed**: the STINGAllo API it calls is rate-limited (100 requests per IP per day), so the agent does not get it |
| `docs/tool_cards/P31_query_opentarget_genetics.md` | the tool `query_opentarget_genetics` | it is registered but **not exposed**: the upstream host `api.genetics.opentargets.org` no longer resolves (the card records this) |

The 45 exposed tools each have exactly one card, and every one of the
45 names in `alloagent/exposed_tools.txt` has a card. The remaining 45
cards are the exposed tools, so the count of the **cards of exposed
tools** is 45 and the count of the **files in `docs/tool_cards/`** is 48.
The tool cards of the two registered-but-not-exposed tools are kept
because they record why the tools are not exposed.

